    <meta name='title' content='nurbs-weights'/>
    <meta name='description' content='Repro for a spec question: X3D 4.0 clause 27 holds NurbsCurve control points and weights in separate fields and sets P.w = weight, but names no convention for whether controlPoint x y z are already multiplied by the weight. Control polygon (0,0) (0.75,1) (1.5,-1) (2.25,1) (3,0), weight 1 1 3 1 1, order 3, default clamped knots, drawn inside a Transform that shifts it 1.5 left (the control points themselves are not shifted). Gold spheres (first file only): where C(u) = sum N P / sum N w puts u = 0.5 (0.60,-0.20) and the right peak (2.09,0.41). Maroon spheres: where the Piegl-Tiller C(u) = sum N w P / sum N w puts them, (1.50,-0.80) and (2.49,0.30). The maroon dotted line is the Piegl-Tiller curve, precomputed with numpy. This file writes the control points as plain Cartesian points, as Piegl-Tiller tools export them.'/>
    <meta name='creator' content='HagopJay'/>
    <meta name='generator' content='hand-written Python generator, X3D research showcase'/>
